From 55383df8aeefdebfa104ec97534557f2e05fb784 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:38:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] doc/examples/remux: log input packets before remapping the
 stream index

log_packet() looks up the time base in the given format context by
pkt->stream_index. The "in" line was printed after stream_index had
already been replaced by the index of the output stream, so whenever
an input stream is skipped (data and attachment streams are not
remuxed), the packets of all following streams were logged with the
index and the time base of the wrong input stream.

For example, with a MOV file holding video, a tmcd data track and
audio, the audio packets were printed as

  in: pts:1024 pts_time:40.96 ... stream_index:1

using the 1/25 time base of the data track, instead of

  in: pts:1024 pts_time:0.02322 ... stream_index:2

Log the packet before the index is remapped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 doc/examples/remux.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/examples/remux.c b/doc/examples/remux.c
index fc63707..78e2126 100644
--- a/doc/examples/remux.c
+++ b/doc/examples/remux.c
@@ -158,9 +158,10 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
             continue;
         }
 
+        log_packet(ifmt_ctx, pkt, "in");
+
         pkt->stream_index = stream_mapping[pkt->stream_index];
         out_stream = ofmt_ctx->streams[pkt->stream_index];
-        log_packet(ifmt_ctx, pkt, "in");
 
         /* copy packet */
         av_packet_rescale_ts(pkt, in_stream->time_base, out_stream->time_base);
